.TH PERSEPOLIS-RENAME 1 "2026-10-10" "persepolis-rename.py" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
persepolis-rename \- fix RFC 5987-encoded filenames from Persepolis downloads
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B persepolis-rename.py
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B persepolis-rename.py
scans
.I ~/Downloads/Persepolis
and subfolders (Videos, Compressed, Audios, Documents, Others), decoding
filenames stuck in the form
.IR '"; filename*=UTF\-8\'\'<url\-encoded>' .
.P
Skips files still open (via
.BR fuser (1)),
files with an active
.I .persepolis
sidecar, and targets that already exist. On rename it also fixes the sidecar
JSON
.I file_name
field and updates the Persepolis sqlite database. Takes no arguments.
.SH OPTIONS
None. Takes no flags or arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
Clean up after a download batch:
.IP
.EX
persepolis-rename.py
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Completed; prints how many files were renamed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Downloads/Persepolis
Scan root.
.TP
.I ~/.config/persepolis_download_manager/persepolis.db
Download database updated on each rename.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fuser (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
